WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.430
- [Dan] In a lot of neighborhoods,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.730
the public park is the
center of the community

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.990
and the basketball court is
the center of that public park.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.390
Oftentimes, these courts,
they're in rough shape.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.240
There's courts where
either there's no lines

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.100
or where there's large gaps

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.240
and cracks in the court's surface.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.870
There can be huge dips
that would be unsafe,

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.660
hazardous to play on.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.750
So seein' all these courts across the city

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.840
inspired me to renovate public
outdoor basketball courts

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.970
and collaborate with artists

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.270
to create unique works
of art for the surface.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.090
- [Karo] I pretty much played
at this court my whole life.

00:00:38.046 --> 00:00:38.900
It was a no-brainer for me.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.050
Like, I jumped at the opportunity
to be able to come down

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.710
and help paint and give
back to the community.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.543
(classical music)

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.430
- [Dan] Lincoln Park is
a special court for me

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:00.900
because I actually used to
play here when I was in school.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.800
All my siblings grew up
playing on this court,

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.203
and so this court's
been a long time coming.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.720
The actual process of renovating the court

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.170
typically takes about two weeks,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.170
and usually they'll hire
a local contracting crew

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.500
to do any crack fill or patch repair.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.740
And then after they've done that,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.320
we come in once the
court has been resurfaced

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.670
to get the artwork down
and be ready for lines.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.680
Since starting Project Backboard
three and a half years ago,

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.280
we worked on over two dozen
courts around the world.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:32.980
One of the most fun parts

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:35.480
is working with community
volunteers on the court painting.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.650
You're gonna start at the tape line

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.240
and we're gonna work our way backwards.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.570
You know, the basketball court, for me,

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:42.320
was always a place where

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.990
you learned to be an engaged citizen.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.100
It's where you met your neighbors

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.040
and kind of got together
for a common purpose.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.790
And I think, too often, people
think of basketball courts

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.480
as a nuisance, when really it is a spot

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.180
that can really bring people
and communities together.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.430
- [Karo] Before this, it was
cracks all over the court,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.550
graffiti everywhere,
definitely in bad shape.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.570
Giving back to the community
kind of speaks to me

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.240
because this is my first time

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.210
kind of being involved
in a project like this,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.240
and it definitely inspires other kids

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.760
due to the fact that, you know,

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.260
the younger generation always looks up

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.670
to the older generation.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.683
They see you giving back, it
will inspire them to give back.

00:02:20.066 --> 00:02:21.520
(basketball net swishing)

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.110
Being able to step on a new
renovated court is pretty dope.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.170
You know, know it seems small,
just a basketball court,

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.378
but, you know, it's a lot more than that.

00:02:27.378 --> 00:02:28.630
Everyone comes out.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.740
People get off work.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.260
Got people who don't
even live in New Rochelle

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.720
who come over here to watch the games,

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.803
so definitely just the little
things helps out a lot.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.320
- [Dan] This didn't
start as an art project.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.910
It didn't start as a way
to bring art into parks.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.370
But I think I recognize
that it's really important

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.470
for me to inspire and help others

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.850
do this in their own communities.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.060
You know, I want people to feel like

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.110
I can make a difference in my community.

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.320
Maybe I'm not painting an
entire basketball court.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.540
Maybe I'm just buying new nets

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.910
and hanging them when they fall down.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.520
Maybe I'm just picking up the trash.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.440
You know, whatever it is, it's,
if you care about your park,

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.820
you care about your basketball
court, take care of it.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.886
(basketball net swishing)

00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:10.719
(classical music)

